WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:06.009
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and Ben Wheatley
who’s directing the first two episodes of

00:00:06.009 --> 00:00:12.410
Series 8 said that this year stories will
be much more like classic who, by which he

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:14.630
means dark and amazing.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:23.300
I spent all last night thinking about walking
dead so now I’m imagining the tardis landing

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.539
inside the prison.

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:28.000
Doctor Who has done zombie stories by the
way.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.150
Last week I also said I’d talk a little
about the things we learned from the out door

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:34.810
scenes peter capaldi and jenna louise coleman
filmed.

00:00:34.810 --> 00:00:37.620
As always I’ll be picking the best questions
out of the comments to answer in my next Q&amp;A

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:44.530
video, if you’re finding me for the first
time be sure to subscribe to get it!

00:00:44.530 --> 00:00:47.300
Don’t you just feel like everyone is going
to rush to netflix to start re-watching all

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.300
the old stuff now.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.130
So here are 5 important takeaways from the
Wheatley’s Interview.

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:53.410
Number 5 - Think of Tom Baker’s run.

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:58.090
The tone of his run is specifically mentioned
and the season 15 finale invasion of time

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.750
when the fourth doctor left his companion
leela behind on gallifrey.

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:04.660
That was also one of the rare moments a doctor
broke the fourth wall and addressed the camera

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:05.660
directly.

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:10.909
Number 4 - Capaldi is a Scholar of Doctor
Who.

00:01:10.909 --> 00:01:14.579
As opposed to Matt Smith who came to the role
with a completely fresh perspective, Capaldi

00:01:14.579 --> 00:01:17.189
has been watching Doctor Who since he was
a little boy.

00:01:17.189 --> 00:01:20.079
He even got to go on set and meet the Third
Doctor during his run.

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:23.819
He’s an amazing actor, so he won’t be
copying any of the classic doctor’s, but

00:01:23.819 --> 00:01:27.499
I take his pre-existing knowledge of the series
to mean that we’ll see a lot of familiar

00:01:27.499 --> 00:01:28.499
traits.

00:01:28.499 --> 00:01:32.490
So if you see a little bit of your favorite
classic doctor’s in his performance, it’s

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:33.920
completely intentional.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:40.119
Number 3 - Most recently Wheatley has been
working on horror stories.

00:01:40.119 --> 00:01:41.119
J.G.

00:01:41.119 --> 00:01:42.229
Ballad’s High Rise to be specific.

00:01:42.229 --> 00:01:45.970
What does it tell you when Doctor Who is being
directed by someone enamoured with the 70s

00:01:45.970 --> 00:01:46.970
horror genre?

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:50.829
That we’re going to get some old school
looking horror doctor who.

00:01:50.829 --> 00:01:52.039
Or at least some really scary stories if not
outright horror.

00:01:52.039 --> 00:01:55.490
Number 2 - Capaldi is still developing his
Doctor character.

00:01:55.490 --> 00:01:59.459
Filming each episode happens fairly quickly,
so it doesn’t leave a lot of time beforehand

00:01:59.459 --> 00:02:01.630
to completely develop his new persona.

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:04.259
So we’ll probably be seeing that happen
over the course of series 8.

00:02:04.259 --> 00:02:07.340
It’s always a lot of fun to watch how different
Doctor’s have changed over the course of

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:08.340
their runs.

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:11.849
David Tennant and Matt Smith just kept getting
angrier and angrier.

00:02:11.849 --> 00:02:14.540
So I can’t wait to see Capaldi finally explode.

00:02:14.540 --> 00:02:15.780
Not literally.

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:20.790
and the number 1 takeaway He will be the darkest
doctor we’ve ever seen.

00:02:20.790 --> 00:02:24.860
All the valeyard theorists will enjoy this,
even though I don’t think he’s the valeyard.

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:29.400
Whatever his performance ends up looking like,
he will essentially be the darkest scariest

00:02:29.400 --> 00:02:31.530
version of the doctor we’ve ever seen.

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:35.170
That by itself sounds so exciting to me that
I think even the most loyal of classic who

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:38.500
fans will enjoy modern who.

00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:43.201
Based on the idea of a really scary dark doctor,
let me know what kinds of stories you’d

00:02:43.201 --> 00:02:44.260
like to see.

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:45.769
Think classic sci-fi horror.

00:02:45.769 --> 00:02:49.120
I’ll be including my favorite comments in
my next Q&amp;A video.

00:02:49.120 --> 00:02:52.021
Now let’s talk about the big rumor we learned
last week from behind the scenes of Series

00:02:52.021 --> 00:02:53.021
8.

00:02:53.021 --> 00:02:54.769
Careful for spoilers if you don’t want to
know.

00:02:54.769 --> 00:02:59.200
It was said that there was some dialogue between
capaldi and jenna louise coleman that implied

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.110
Matt Smith’s doctor had made a phone call
to himself in the future.

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:04.170
to Capaldi’s doctor.

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:08.270
It’s kind of meant to serve as an epilogue
for matt smith, like one final goodbye.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:09.959
He doesn’t appear on screen.

00:03:09.959 --> 00:03:12.719
So if it’s true, it would only be a voice
over cameo.

00:03:12.719 --> 00:03:16.579
But it would make sense given the amount of
time Matt Smith spent talking to handles about

00:03:16.579 --> 00:03:18.540
fixing the phone during the christmas special.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:22.170
If there’s anything I think steven moffat
does really well, it’s paying off minor

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:25.420
story points in really big ways.

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:29.620
River Song was originally just a guest character
until Moffat magicked her into the character

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:30.620
she is now.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:33.110
Let me know what you think about the idea
of Matt Smith having a voice over during the

00:03:33.110 --> 00:03:34.190
series 8 premiere.

